### Volume filesystem needs inspection
Portworx's filesystem check found errors that it can't fix safely on its own (filesystem health 3). Mounting or resizing the volume can fail until they are fixed.

#### Check first
`kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl volume check status <volume>`.

#### Fix
1. Stop the workload that uses the volume.
2. Run `kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl volume check start --mode check_health <volume>` to see the errors, then `kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl volume check start --mode fix_all <volume>` if you accept the repairs. `fix_all` can discard damaged data, so take a snapshot first.
